# trajectory-viz environment variables.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` at the project root and edit values as needed:
#
#     cp docs/env.example .env       # Docker auto-loads .env
#     vim .env
#     docker compose up --build
#
# (.env itself is .gitignore'd — never commit secrets here even though
# this project doesn't use any.)
#
# Each variable lists where it's consumed in the codebase.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PFLOW project root (monorepo mode).
# Consumed by: backend/config.py:get_pflow_home() → falls back to ~/Dropbox/PFLOW
# Required when ingesting from the live PFLOW workspace (i.e. when
# PFLOW_VIZ_DB is NOT set). Unused in standalone mode.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PFLOW_HOME=/path/to/PFLOW

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Absolute path to the DuckDB file the backend reads from.
# Consumed by: backend/config.py:get_viz_db_path()
# When set, takes precedence over PFLOW_HOME — this is the "standalone mode"
# switch. The Docker image defaults this to /data/pflow.duckdb.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PFLOW_VIZ_DB=/path/to/pflow.duckdb

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Root directory that ingest scans for trips/ and trajectory/ subtrees.
# Consumed by: backend/config.py:get_output_root()
# Defaults to ${PFLOW_HOME}/output. Set explicitly if your simulation outputs
# live somewhere else (e.g. a fast SSD or external drive).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PFLOW_VIZ_OUTPUT_ROOT=/path/to/output

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to the sources.yaml declarative-source registry.
# Consumed by: backend/sources_schema.py:default_sources_path()
# Defaults to <project root>/sources.yaml. Override when running multiple
# trajectory-viz instances against the same code with different source sets.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PFLOW_VIZ_SOURCES=/path/to/sources.yaml

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backend HTTP host + port.
# Consumed by: backend/app.py:serve() (used by `trajectory-viz-serve` entry).
# In Docker the defaults are 0.0.0.0:8080 (set in Dockerfile ENV). Native
# `trajectory-viz-serve` defaults to 127.0.0.1:9999 to match Vite proxy.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TRAJECTORY_VIZ_HOST=127.0.0.1
# TRAJECTORY_VIZ_PORT=9999

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend API base (Vite build-time variable; not used at runtime).
# Consumed by: frontend/src/api.ts (import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE)
# In dev mode, Vite proxies /api/* to localhost:9999. In production builds
# served from a different origin than the backend, set this to the backend's
# URL (e.g. https://api.example.org).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_API_BASE=https://api.example.org
